{
  "_comment": "VS Code workspace settings template for the VibeCoded Orchestrator. Copy this to .vscode/settings.json and customize as needed. This file is for VS Code editor preferences (Pylance excludes, file-watcher excludes, formatter settings, etc.) — it is NOT the per-project MCP env channel.",

  "_comment_mcp_env": "The historical claude-code.env block was removed in v0.2.12 (PR-27, 2026-05-16). As of Claude Code 2.1.143 on Linux, .vscode/settings.json claude-code.env does NOT propagate to MCP subprocesses — empirical sentinel testing confirmed this. The canonical channel for per-project MCP env (KG_COLLECTION, PROJECT_NAME, ACTIVE_EMBEDDING, MCP server paths, etc.) is .claude/settings.json env. The VCT launcher writes that file for you when you register a project; if you're setting up manually, see docs/CONFIGURATION.md for the schema. See PR-27 commit message and docs/CLAUDE_CODE_COMPATIBILITY.md → 'Per-project env files' for the full empirical trace and downstream consequences.",

  "_comment_pylance_excludes": "Sample Pylance + file-watcher excludes — the launcher's vco_lib._backfill_vscode_excludes_in_project ships these on install/update. Uncomment if you want them in a hand-managed workspace.",

  "_files_watcherExclude_example": {
    "**/.git/objects/**": true,
    "**/node_modules/**": true,
    "**/__pycache__/**": true,
    "**/.venv/**": true,
    "**/target/**": true
  },

  "_python_analysis_exclude_example": [
    "**/.venv/**",
    "**/__pycache__/**",
    "**/.mypy_cache/**"
  ]
}
